Riad Al Sunbati that brought these quatrains to life. Through new arrangements and original compositions by Tabassian, the project creates a vibrant dialogue between centuries-old Sufi poetry and the sounds of today, bridging Arab and Persian musical traditions.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Tonhalle\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Museumstrasse 25, 9000 St. Gallen, Suisse\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Konzert und Theater St Gallen\",\"url\":\"https://www.konzertundtheater.ch/\"}]}\n\t\t\t\t03jul19 h 00 minKhayyam & Oum KalthoumWhereSt Gallen, Switzerland\n\t\t\t\t\t\n    Event DetailsKiya Tabassian and his ensemble Constantinople present a contemporary reinterpretation of the Rubaiyat, the renowned collection of poems by Persian poet, astronomer, and mathematician Omar Khayyam. In collaboration    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Kiya Tabassian and his ensemble Constantinople present a contemporary reinterpretation of the Rubaiyat, the renowned collection of poems by Persian poet, astronomer, and mathematician Omar Khayyam. In collaboration with singer Ghalia Benali, they pay tribute to the legacy of Umm Kulthum, the iconic voice of Middle Eastern music, by revisiting the compositions of Riad Al Sunbati that brought these quatrains to life. Through new arrangements and original compositions by Tabassian, the project creates a vibrant dialogue between centuries-old Sufi poetry and the sounds of today, bridging Arab and Persian musical traditions.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy your ticketsBook your tickets here\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOn stage\n\nKiya Tabassian,  setar, voice and artistic direction\nGhalia Benali, voice\nDidem Basar, qanun\nCharbel Rouhana, oud\nNeva Özgen, kemenche\nAmanda Keesmaat, baroque violin\nTanya LaPerrière, viola d’amore\nJavier Núñez, positive organ\nVincent Noiret, doublebass\nPatrick Graham, percussion\nHamin Honari, percussion\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime3 July 2026 19 h 00 min(GMT+02:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationTonhalleMuseumstrasse 25, 9000 St. Gallen, SuisseOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWhereSt Gallen, Switzerland\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tOrganizerKonzert und Theater St GallenLearn More\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCalendarGoogleCal\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tGet Directions\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAddress - Khayyam & Oum Kalthoum []\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tDestination Address - Khayyam & Oum Kalthoum []\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\tKath.PriesterseminarAugustinerstraße 34, 55116 Mainz, Allemagne\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_19313_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Estuary\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://constantinople.ca/en/events/estuary-24/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-7-14T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-7-14T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/estuaire_constantinople_cissokonikolaj_lund_3-2.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>A luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.</strong><br data-start='147' data-end='150' /><br /> With this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and voices embody the beauty of Persian and Mandinka music. Master of the kora Ablaye Cissoko and setâr player Kiya Tabassian immerse us in a gentle sonic reverie. A musica