 setar & voice\nAblaye Cissoko, kora & voice\nPatrick Graham, percussion\nPierre-Yves Martel, viola da gamba\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime9 June 2026 19 h 30 min(GMT+09:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMusashino Civic Cultural Hall3 Chome-9-11 Nakacho, Musashino, Tokyo 180-0006, JaponOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWhereMusashino, Japan\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tOrganizerMusashino Civic Cultural HallLearn More\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCalendarGoogleCal\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tGet Directions\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAddress - Traversées []\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tDestination Address - Traversées []\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\tOrangerieschlossAn d. Orangerie 3-5, 14469 Potsdam, Allemagne\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_19309_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Cantemir, The Composer Prince\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://constantinople.ca/en/events/cantemir-the-composer-prince/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-6-17T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-6-17T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/constantinople_cantemirconstantinople-1.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<div class=''><span class=''>In this creation, Constantinople dedicates itself to the work of Dimitrie Cantemir, an emblematic figure bridging European and Middle Eastern cultures at the dawn of the 18th century.</span></div> <div class=''> <div class='WordSection1'> <div id='mail-editor-reference-message-container' class=''> <div id='mail-editor-reference-message-container' class=''> <p class=''><span class='' style='color: #000000;'><span class='' lang='EN-US'>Cantemir was not only a prince and scholar, but also a renowned composer and diplomat and transcended borders and centuries with his talent. His musical contributions are invaluable: his compositions are gems of Ottoman music, showcasing the empire&#8217;s richness and diversity at its peak. Moreover, Cantemir&#8217;s meticulous compilation and transcription work in the monumental &#8220;Edvar-i Musiki&#8221; stand unparalleled. With over 350 meticulously transcribed instrumental pieces, Cantemir&#8217;s collection offers a comprehensive insight into Ottoman and Middle Eastern music of the 16th and 17th centuries, making it a crucial resource for understanding these musical traditions.</span></span></p> <p class=''><span class='' style='color: #000000;'><span class='' lang='EN-US'>Under the artistic direction of Kiya Tabassian, Constantinople approaches Cantemir&#8217;s treasure trove with erudite precision and creative flair. By interpreting Cantemir&#8217;s compositions alongside works by his contemporaries like the French Marin Marais and the Italian Antonio Bertali, the musicians infuse new vitality into these centuries-old pieces, rendering them vivid and tangible for modern audiences.</span></span></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Orangerieschloss\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"An d. Orangerie 3-5, 14469 Potsdam, Allemagne\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Musikfestspiele\",\"url\":\"https://www.musikfestspiele-potsdam.de\"}]}\n\t\t\t\t17jun19 h 00 minCantemir, The Composer PrinceWherePostdam, Germany\n\t\t\t\t\t\n    Event DetailsIn this creation, Constantinople dedicates itself to the work of Dimitrie Cantemir, an emblematic figure bridging European and Middle Eastern cultures at the dawn of the 18th century.    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                In this creation, Constantinople dedicates itself to the work of Dimitrie Cantemir, an emblematic figure bridging European and Middle Eastern cultures at the dawn of the 18th century.\n\n\n\n\nCantemir was not only a prince and scholar, but also a renowned composer and diplomat and transcended borders and centuries with his talent. His musical contributions are invaluable: his compositions are gems of Ottoman music, showcasing the empire’s richness and diversity at its peak. Moreover, Cantemir’s meticulous compilation and transcription work in the monumental “Edvar-i Musiki” stand unparalleled. With over 350 meticulously transcribed instrumental pieces, Cantemir’s collection offers a comprehensive insight into Ottoman and Middle Eastern music of the 16th and 17th centuries, making it a crucial resource for understanding these musical traditions.\nUnder the artistic direction of Kiya Tabassian, Constantinople approaches Cantemir’s treasure trove with erudite precision and creative flair. By interpreting Cantemir’s compositions alongside works by his contemporaries like the French Marin Marais and the Italian Antonio Bertali, the musicians infuse new vitality into these centuries-old pieces, rendering them vivid and tangible for modern audiences.\n\n\n\n\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy your ticketsBook your tickets here\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOn stage\nKiya Tabassian, setar and direction\nKianoush Khalilian, ney\nDidem Basar, kanun\nTanya LaPerrière, baroque violin and viola d’amore\nPatrick Graham, percussions\nMichel Angers, theorbe\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime17 June 2026 19 h 00 min(GMT+02:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationOrangerieschlossAn d. Orangerie 3-5, 14469 Potsdam, AllemagneOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWherePostdam, Germany\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tOrganizerMusikfestspieleLear