cussion, had always existed side by side.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy your ticketsBook your tickets here\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOn stage\nKiya Tabassian, setar & voice\nAblaye Cissoko, kora & voice\nPatrick Graham, percussion\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime18 June 2026 20 h 00 min(GMT+02:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMetzgplatz, Lenzburg5600 Lenzburg, SuisseOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWhereLenzburg, Switzerland\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCalendarGoogleCal\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tGet Directions\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAddress - Traversées []\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tDestination Address - Traversées []\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\tGrand Bazaar IstanbulBeyazıt, 34126 Fatih/İstanbul, Turquie\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_19411_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Fleeting Beauties\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://constantinople.ca/en/events/fleeting-beauties-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-6-21T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-6-21T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/il-ponte-3-juan-manuel-lobaton-web.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p class='font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]'>As part of the Istanbul Music Festival, Constantinople takes over one of the city&#8217;s most historically rich venues: the Grand Bazaar. A crossroads of trade routes for centuries, this iconic space hosts the concert &#8220;Fleeting Beauties&#8221; — an invitation to experience music as a fleeting and precious encounter between different eras and geographies.</p> <p class='font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]'>The programme features music ranging from the Italian Renaissance to Ottoman and Iranian repertoires, brought together for one evening to reveal the fragile beauty of each musical moment. Alongside counter-tenor Marco Beasley, Constantinople explores this living plurality in which each work exists fully only in the moment of its performance.</p> <p class='font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]'>A unique concert, at the heart of a unique place.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Grand Bazaar Istanbul\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Beyazıt, 34126 Fatih/İstanbul, Turquie\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Istanbul Muzik Festival\",\"url\":\"https://muzik.iksv.org/tr\"}]}\n\t\t\t\t21jun19 h 00 minFleeting BeautiesWhereIstanbul, Türkyie\n\t\t\t\t\t\n    Event DetailsAs part of the Istanbul Music Festival, Constantinople takes over one of the city’s most historically rich venues: the Grand Bazaar. A crossroads of trade routes    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                As part of the Istanbul Music Festival, Constantinople takes over one of the city’s most historically rich venues: the Grand Bazaar. A crossroads of trade routes for centuries, this iconic space hosts the concert “Fleeting Beauties” — an invitation to experience music as a fleeting and precious encounter between different eras and geographies.\nThe programme features music ranging from the Italian Renaissance to Ottoman and Iranian repertoires, brought together for one evening to reveal the fragile beauty of each musical moment. Alongside counter-tenor Marco Beasley, Constantinople explores this living plurality in which each work exists fully only in the moment of its performance.\nA unique concert, at the heart of a unique place.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy your ticketsBook your tickets here\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOn stage\n\nKiya Tabassian, setar, voice & artistic direction\nMarco Beasley, tenor\nDidem Basar, qanun\nPatrick Graham, percussion\nJudith Steenbrink, baroque violin \nFabio Accurso, luth\nMarco Ferrari, flute and ney\nMichel Angers, theorbo\nNeva Özgen, kemenche\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime21 June 2026 19 h 00 min(GMT+03:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationGrand Bazaar IstanbulBeyazıt, 34126 Fatih/İstanbul, TurquieOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWhereIstanbul, Türkyie\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tOrganizerIstanbul Muzik FestivalLearn More\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCalendarGoogleCal\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tGet Directions\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAddress - Fleeting Beauties []\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tDestination Address - Fleeting Beauties []\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\tBasilica di San VitaleVia San Vitale, 17, 48121 Ravenna RA, Italie\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_19311_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Estuary\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://constantinople.ca/en/events/estuary-23/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-6-23T21:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-6-23T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/estuaire_constantinople_cissokonikolaj_lund_3-2.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>A luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.</strong><br data-start='147' data-end='150' /><br /> With this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and voices embody the beauty of Persian and Mandinka music. Master of the kora Ablaye Cissoko and setâr player Kiya Tabassian immerse us in a gentle sonic reverie. A musical conversation at its finest, elevated by the rhythms and subtleties of percussionist Patrick Graham. Inspired by the estuary—this space of transition and transformation—three exceptional artists craft a vast palette of colors with cosmopolitan accents.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Basilica di San Vitale\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Via San Vitale, 17, 48121 Ravenna RA, Italie\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Ravenna Festival\",\"url\":\"https://www.ravennafestival.org/\"}]}\n\t\t\t\t23jun21 h 30 minEstuaryWhereRavenna, Italy\n\t\t\t\t\t\n    Event DetailsA luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.\nWith this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                A luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.\nWith this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and voices embody the beauty of Persian and Mandinka music. Master of the kora Ablaye Cissoko and setâr player Kiya Tabassian immerse us in a gentle sonic reverie. A musical conversation at its finest, elevated by the rhythms and subtleties of percussionist Patrick Graham. Inspired by the estuary—this space of transition and transformation—three exceptional artists craft a vast palette of colors with cosmopolitan accents.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy your ticketsBook your tickets here\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOn stage\nKiya Tabassian, setar & voice\nAblaye Cissoko, kora & voice\nPatrick Graham, percussion\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime23 June 2026 21 h 30 min(GMT+02:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationBasilica di San VitaleVia San Vitale, 17, 48121 Ravenna RA, ItalieOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWhereRavenna, Italy\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tOrganizerRavenna FestivalLearn More\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCalendarGoogleCal\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tGet Directions\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAddress - Estuary []\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tDestination Address - Estuary []\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\tJuly 2026TonhalleMuseumstrasse 25, 9000 St. Gallen, Suisse\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_19547_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Khayyam &amp; Oum Kalthoum\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://constantinople.ca/en/events/khayyam-oum-kalthoum-3/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-7-3T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-7-3T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/khayyam_oukalthoumjefberhin_halo.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Kiya Tabassian and his ensemble Constantinople present a contemporary reinterpretation of the <em data-start='111' data-end='121'>Rubaiyat</em>, the renowned collection of poems by Persian poet, astronomer, and mathematician Omar Khayyam. In collaboration with singer Ghalia Benali, they pay tribute to the legacy of Umm Kulthum, the iconic voice of Middle Eastern music, by revisiting the compositions of Riad Al Sunbati that brought these quatrains to life. Through new arrangements and original compositions by Tabassian, the project creates a vibrant dialogue between centuries-old Sufi poetry and the sounds of today, bridging Arab and Persian musical traditions.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Tonhalle\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Museumstrasse 25, 9000 St. Gallen, Suisse\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Konzert und Theater St Gallen\",\"url\":\"https://www.konzertundtheater.ch/\"}]}\n\t\t\t\t03jul19 h 00 minKhayyam & Oum KalthoumWhereSt Gallen, Switzerland\n\t\t\t\t\t\n    Event DetailsKiya Tabassian and his ensemble Constantinople present a contemporary reinterpretation of the Rubaiyat, the renowned collection of poems by Persian poet, astronomer, and mathematician Omar Khayyam. In collaboration    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Kiya Tabassian and his ensemble Constantinople present a contemporary reinterpretation of the Rubaiyat, the renowned collection of poems by Persian poet, astronomer, and mathematician Omar Khayyam. In collaboration with singer Ghalia Benali, they pay tribute to the legacy of Umm Kulthum, the iconic voice of Middle Eastern music, by revisiting the compositions of Riad Al Sunbati that brought these quatrains to life. Through new arrangements and original compositions by Tabassian, the project creates a vibrant dialogue between centuries-old Sufi poetry and the sounds of today, bridging Arab and Persian musical traditions.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy your ticketsBook your tickets here\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOn stage\n\nKiya Tabassian,  setar, voice and artistic direction\nGhalia Benali, voice\nDidem Basar, qanun\nCharbel Rouhana, oud\nNeva Özgen, kemenche\nAmanda Keesmaat, baroque violin\nTanya LaPerrière, viola d’amore\nJavier Núñez, positive organ\nVincent Noiret, doublebass\nPatrick Graham, percussion\nHamin Honari, percussion\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime3 July 2026 19 h 00 min(GMT+02:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationTonhalleMuseumstrasse 25, 9000 St. Gallen, SuisseOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWhereSt Gallen, Switzerland\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tOrganizerKonzert und Theater St GallenLearn More\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCalendarGoogleCal\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tGet Directions\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAddress - Khayyam & Oum Kalthoum []\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tDestination Address - Khayyam & Oum Kalthoum []\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\tKath.PriesterseminarAugustinerstraße 34, 55116 Mainz, Allemagne\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_19313_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Estuary\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://constantinople.ca/en/events/estuary-24/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-7-14T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-7-14T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/estuaire_constantinople_cissokonikolaj_lund_3-2.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>A luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.</strong><br data-start='147' data-end='150' /><br /> With this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and voices embody the beauty of Persian and Mandinka music. Master of the kora Ablaye Cissoko and setâr player Kiya Tabassian immerse us in a gentle sonic reverie. A musical conversation at its finest, elevated by the rhythms and subtleties of percussionist Patrick Graham. Inspired by the estuary—this space of transition and transformation—three exceptional artists craft a vast palette of colors with cosmopolitan accents.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Kath.Priesterseminar\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Augustinerstraße 34, 55116 Mainz, Allemagne\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Mainz Klassik\",\"url\":\"https://www.mainz-klassik.de/\"}]}\n\t\t\t\t14jul19 h 30 minEstuaryWhereMainz, Germany\n\t\t\t\t\t\n    Event DetailsA luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.\nWith this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                A luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.\nWith this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and voices embody the beauty of Persian and Mandinka music. Master of the kora Ablaye Cissoko and setâr player Kiya Tabassian immerse us in a gentle sonic reverie. A musical conversation at its finest, elevated by the rhythms and subtleties of percussionist Patrick Graham. Inspired by the estuary—this space of transition and transformation—three exceptional artists craft a vast palette of colors with cosmopolitan accents.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy your ticketsBook your tickets here\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOn stage\nKiya Tabassian, setar & voice\nAblaye Cissoko, kora & voice\nPatrick Graham, percussion\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime14 July 2026 19 h 30 min(GMT+02:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationKath.PriesterseminarAugustinerstraße 34, 55116 Mainz, AllemagneOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWhereMainz, Germany\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tOrganizerMainz KlassikLearn More\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCalendarGoogleCal\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tGet Directions\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAddress - Estuary []\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tDestination Address - Estuary []\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\tPilgrimage Church of the Assumption of the Virgin MaryU Kostela 1, 382 21 Kájov, Tchéquie\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_19315_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Harant&#039;s Odyssey\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://constantinople.ca/en/events/harants-odyssey-14/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-7-23T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-7-23T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/krytof-harant-4-petra-hajska-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>A musical journey into the world of Czech composer Kryštof Harant (1564-1621) and his travel book that details his odyssey from Prague to Jerusalem by way of Venice, Cyprus, Sinai and Cairo. The internationally renowned vocal ensemble Cappella Mariana and Constantinople join forces to revisit Harant’s music and the music he would have heard on his extraordinary 17th-century expedition.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Pilgrimage Church of the Assumption of the Virgin Mary\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"U Kostela 1, 382 21 Kájov, Tchéquie\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Festival Krumlov\",\"url\":\"https://www.festivalkrumlov.cz/\"}]}\n\t\t\t\t23jul19 h 30 minHarant's OdysseyWhereKajov, Czechia\n\t\t\t\t\t\n    Event DetailsA musical journey into the world of Czech composer Kryštof Harant (1564-1621) and his travel book that details his odyssey from Prague to Jerusalem by way of Venice, Cyprus, Sinai    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                A musical journey into the world of Czech composer Kryštof Harant (1564-1621) and his travel book that details his odyssey from Prague to Jerusalem by way of Venice, Cyprus, Sinai and Cairo. The internationally renowned vocal ensemble Cappella Mariana and Constantinople join forces to revisit Harant’s music and the music he would have heard on his extraordinary 17th-century expedition.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tBuy your ticketsBook your tickets here\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tOn stageCappella Mariana (Czech Republic)\nVojtěch Semerád – direction, tenor  \nHana Blažíková – soprano \nBarbora Kabátková – soprano \nTomáš Lajtkep – tenor \nOndrej Holub – tenor \nJaromír Nosek – bass \n& \nConstantinople \nKiya Tabassian – direction, setar et voice \nDidem Başar – kanun \nPatrick Graham – percussion \nNeva Özgen – kemençe \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tTime23 July 2026 19 h 30 min(GMT+02:00)\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationPilgrimage Church of the Assumption of the Virgin MaryU Kostela 1, 382 21 Kájov, TchéquieOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tWhereKajov, Czechia\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tOrganizerFestival KrumlovLearn More\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCalendarGoogleCal\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\tGet Directions\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAddress - Harant's Odyssey []\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tDestination Address - Harant's Odyssey []\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\tNovember 2026Le Rocher de Palmer1 Rue Aristide Briand, 33152 Cenon\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_19660_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Estuary\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://constantinople.ca/en/events/estuary-25/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-11-10T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-11-10T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/estuaire_constantinople_cissokonikolaj_lund_3-2.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>A luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.</strong><br data-start='147' data-end='150' /><br /> With this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and voices embody the beauty of Persian and Mandinka music. Master of the kora Ablaye Cissoko and setâr player Kiya Tabassian immerse us in a gentle sonic reverie. A musical conversation at its finest, elevated by the rhythms and subtleties of percussionist Patrick Graham. Inspired by the estuary—this space of transition and transformation—three exceptional artists craft a vast palette of colors with cosmopolitan accents.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Le Rocher de Palmer\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"1 Rue Aristide Briand, 33152 Cenon\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Constantinople\"}]}\n\t\t\t\t10nov20 h 30 minEstuaryWhereBordeaux, France\n\t\t\t\t\t\n    Event DetailsA luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.\nWith this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and    \n        \n     