    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                A luminous encounter of kindred musicians: between poetry and inspired musical dialogue.\nWith this ensemble that has traveled the world’s stages for over a decade, strings and voices embody the beauty of Persian and Mandinka music. Master of the kora Ablaye Cissoko and setâr player Kiya Tabassian immerse us in a gentle sonic reverie. A musical conversation at its finest, elevated by the rhythms and subtleties of percussionist Patrick Graham. Inspired by the estuary—this space of transition and transformation—three exceptional artists craft a vast palette of colors with cosmopolitan accents.\n            "
      }
