  {
    "@id": "https://constantinople.ca/en/events/songs-of-hope-13/event_18910_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://constantinople.ca/en/events/accross-the-andes/var/ri-0.l-L2"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://constantinople.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/traversee_andes_federico_tarazonamichael_slobodian-1-e1758123326837.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/organizer": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g17679240"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://constantinople.ca/en/events/songs-of-hope-13/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "ACCROSS THE ANDES"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>ACCROSS THE ANDES</p> <p>Exploring the Musical Heritage of Peru</p> <p>The music of the Andes and South America is heir to pre-His­panic musical traditions, which were enriched by the contribu­tion of instruments and repertoires of the peoples who settled the lands of this “New World.” This interaction between vastly different cultures gave rise to the most remarkable music, which was rediscovered in codices from the 16th and 17th centuries and which have seen the addition of pieces from oral and popular tra­ditions that were passed down from one generation to the next. We invite you to a musical evening filled with light and colour, in the company of Constantinople’s musicians and Federico Tarazona, one of the greatest virtuosos of the most symbolic and representative instrument of Andean music, the charango.</p> <p>This project is supported financially by the Conseil des Arts et des Lettres du Québec, the Conseil des Arts du Canada, and the Asociación ZINIA in Peru.</p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-5-25T20:00-4::00"
      }
